==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|scrutny}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|scrutiny|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|ML.|en}} {{term|scrutinium|scrūtinium|a search, an inquiry|lang=la}}, from {{etyl|VL.|en}} {{term|scrutari|scrūtārī|to search or examine thoroughly|lang=la}}, of uncertain origin. Possibly from {{etyl|LL.|en}} {{term|scruta|scrūta|rubbish, broken trash|lang=la}}; or of {{etyl|gem|en}} origin, related to {{etyl|ang|en}} {{term|scrutnung|scrūtnung|examination, investigation, inquiry, search|lang=ang}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{term|scrutnian|scrūtnian|lang=ang}}, {{term|scrudnian|scrūdnian|to examine carefully, scrutinize, consider, investigate|lang=ang}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{recons|skrudōną|lang=gem-pro}}, {{recons|skruþōną||to search, examine|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{recons|skrud-|lang=gem-pro}}, {{recons|skruþ-||to cut|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{recons|(s)kreut-||to cut|lang=ine-pro}}. Compare {{etyl|goh|-}} {{term|skrodon|skrodōn|lang=goh}}, {{term|scruton|scrutōn|lang=goh}}, {{term|scrutilon|scrutilōn|to research, explore|lang=goh}}, {{etyl|goh|-}} {{term|scrod||a search, scrutiny|lang=goh}}, {{etyl|got|-}} {{term|||tr=andhruskan|to investigate, explore|lang=got}}, {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term|screadian|scrēadian|to shred, cut up, cut off, peel, pare, prune|lang=ang}}. More at {{l|en|shred}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈskɹuː.tɪ.niː/}}, {{X-SAMPA|/"skru:.tI.ni:/}}
* {{hyphenation|scru|ti|ny}}
* {{audio|en-us-scrutiny.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|scrutin|ies}}

# Intense [[study]] of someone or something.
#* Milton
#*: Thenceforth I thought thee worth my nearer view / And narrower '''scrutiny'''.
# Thorough [[inspection]] of a situation or a case.
# An [[examination]] of [[catechumen]]s, in the last week of [[Lent]], who were to receive [[baptism]] on [[Easter]] Day.
# A [[ticket]], or little paper [[billet]], on which a [[vote]] is written.
# An examination by a [[committee]] of the votes given at an election, for the purpose of correcting the [[poll]].
#: {{rfquotek|Brande & C}}

